;
UPLOADS AND LIBRARY MAINTENANCE

A - Transfers and incoming software

:A
TRANSFERS AND INCOMING SOFTWARE

Try at least one download and one upload yourself. There is no substitute for
having seen the process from the caller's side when someone says his terminal
has hung.

    YSEND A0:WELCOME.TXT
    UPLOAD EXAMPLE.LBR
    UPLOAD /Y

YSEND sends YMODEM; start the corresponding receive operation in your
terminal. UPLOAD filename receives one file using XMODEM/CRC; UPLOAD /Y
receives a YMODEM batch. Start the matching send operation at the terminal
when prompted.

Completed submissions go to uploads/inbox/ on the host. In-progress files go
to uploads/staging/. Keep both on the same filesystem: completion uses an
atomic hard link. Duplicate names receive unique suffixes, rather than
overwriting earlier submissions. Interrupted partial files are discarded;
previously completed batch members remain. XMODEM retains record padding,
while YMODEM retains the declared length.

MESSAGE notes saved by callers also arrive in the inbox. Unsaved drafts are
discarded at call recovery. These files survive WORK cleanup and ordinary
restarts.

Examine the actual contents of a submission, not just its filename. Check
archive members, accompanying documentation and redistribution terms. Retain
the original. Stop the board and back up the destination disk before importing
reviewed files using the correct image format. Never place arbitrary uploaded
files directly in the disk catalog, or automatically approve an uploaded COM
file for caller execution.
